 ### [Helicity Visualization](8393-helicity-visualization.md)
-Helicity Visualization is a scalarization technique for vector fields that maps the dot product of velocity and vorticity to opacity and color to identify vortices. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Metric Scalar Field Rendering from Vector Fields](14065-metric-scalar-field-rendering-from-vector-fields.md) by explicitly leveraging the alignment between flow direction and local rotation (curl) to highlight swirling features, whereas metric methods often rely on magnitude or strain. See [Helicity Visualization](8393-helicity-visualization.md).
