 ### Velocity Component Visualization
-- **Definition**: Visualizing specific components of the velocity field (e.g., x-component) to identify flow separation and reversal [S1, unofficial].
-- **Step**: Map the smallest x velocity values (including negative values) to cyan and high opacity. Map the largest x velocity components to yellow and near transparency [S1, unofficial].
+Visualizing specific components of the velocity field (e.g., x-component) to identify flow separation and reversal [S1, unofficial]. Map the smallest x velocity values (including negative values) to cyan and high opacity. Map the largest x velocity components to yellow and near transparency [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-The technique originated in early computational fluid dynamics (CFD) visualization research. Volume Rendering for Computational Fluid Dynamics: Initial Results (1991) demonstrated the use of scalarization to visualize perturbation velocity fields, specifically mapping negative x-components to cyan to highlight flow separation from surfaces [S1, unofficial].
